{
  "_doc": "A cast-iron box stove (#866; refs experiments/prop_lab/refs/saloon/): the long wood-burning box stove of the 1860s-80s that heated saloons, stores and depots, a firebox 84 cm long on four short cast legs, a door at its +x end with a sliding draught, a collar on its top at the back for the pipe; on a box of sand (old oak boards round it) that keeps the floor from its heat and its coals; its pipe (four 62 cm lengths of 6 in pipe) straight up to the flue: the placing session takes off the lengths the ceiling doesn't want. Iron (`wood` iron: it doesn't burn or break; balls glance); the pipe's lengths stand on each other and come down when the stove goes over. A fire source (`stove`, StoveFire): lit by the hour (as the lamps, 17:00 to 7:00) it glows at its draught; knocked over, or its sand box burnt out from under it, its coals spill round its door and burn on the boards for 300 s (FireSystem.small_fire, 1.4 times a spill's heat). Baked the gun way (tools/blender/props/saloon_s1.py: cast iron black-leaded, rubbed to the iron at its edges, rust where the wet mop has been). ~170 kg of iron and ~135 kg of sand (the kit weighs it ~680: StructureMember.weight counts a hollow member's inside as char, a fifth of the iron, #866). 14 physics bodies (its members) standing. Written by tools/props/saloon.py.",
